checkArguments [SimTalk]
Checks if the parameters passed to the Method designated by the reference operator <&> have a
compatible data type.
Remarks
Use checkArguments to make sure that values, which you or a user of a model you create enters into a
dialog, may be passed to Methods.
Type
Method
Syntax
<&>Method.checkArguments([Argument1:any, ...])´
Parameter
The optional parameters Argument of data type any designate the arguments that are to be checked.
Example
&MyMethod.checkArguments(42,void) 
