hasSyntaxError [SimTalk]
Returns if the source code of the Method designated by the reference operator <&> has syntax errors.
Remarks
The method also applies to user-defined attributes of type method.
Type
Method
Syntax
<&>Method.HasSyntaxError([byref ErrorMessage:string, byref Line:integer]) 
-> boolean
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The optional parameter ErrorMessage of data type string designates a local variable to which Plant
Simulation assigns an error message if the Method contains a syntax error.
If the Method does not contain a syntax error, Plant Simulation assigns an empty string ("") to the local
variable.
• The optional parameter Line of data type integer designates a local variable to which Plant Simulation
assigns the line in which the error is located.
Return Value
The return value has the data type boolean.
Example
var NewSourceCode: string := prompt  -- user input
&MyMethod.Program := NewSourceCode   -- assign new source code
if &MyMethod.HasSyntaxError
   print "syntax error"
else
   MyMethod   -- call the Method and execute the new source code
end
hasSyntaxError [SimTalk]
11-3714 Plant Simulation Help
